00:38:51.780 --> 00:38:52.680
But there's more.
但还有更多。

979
00:38:53.040 --> 00:38:54.760
You thought there wasn't, but there is.
你以为没有了，但其实还有。

980
00:38:54.840 --> 00:38:57.420
No, I actually figured you had something else coming.
不，我其实猜到你还有别的内容要说。

981
00:38:57.560 --> 00:38:58.140
I'm cringing.
我听得尴尬症都犯了。

982
00:38:58.340 --> 00:38:58.780
I'm waiting.
我等着呢。

983
00:38:58.780 --> 00:39:05.360
They have a playroom for couples, single women, and invited single men.
他们有一个供情侣、单身女性和受邀单身男性使用的游戏室。

984
00:39:05.460 --> 00:39:06.060
Oh, Lord.
天哪。

985
00:39:06.200 --> 00:39:07.820
It's open from 10.30 p.m.
开放时间是从晚上10点半

986
00:39:07.920 --> 00:39:08.920
to 3 a.m.
到凌晨3点。

987
00:39:09.220 --> 00:39:11.200
You go wrestle with your friends.
你去和你的朋友们摔跤吧。

988
00:39:11.200 --> 00:39:12.060
I don't know.
我不知道该说什么了。

989
00:39:12.280 --> 00:39:17.640
Most people who stay at the resorts are couples, but they do have single-person rates available.
大多数入住度假村的人都是情侣，但他们也提供单人入住价格。

990
00:39:18.360 --> 00:39:19.740
A few more facts.
还有几个事实。

991
00:39:19.940 --> 00:39:21.380
There is no tipping allowed.
这里不允许给小费。

992
00:39:21.680 --> 00:39:22.680
Who are you tipping?
你要给谁小费？

993
00:39:23.200 --> 00:39:25.580
Your waitstaff, but it's all-inclusive.
给服务员，但这里是全包式的。

994
00:39:25.920 --> 00:39:26.560
Oh, okay.
哦，好吧。

995
00:39:26.560 --> 00:39:31.080
So, I mean, I think that that is an important thing to know because where would you put the money?
所以，我的意思是，我觉得这一点很重要，因为你钱放哪儿呢？

996
00:39:31.540 --> 00:39:31.980
Oh.
哦。

997
00:39:32.060 --> 00:39:32.500
You're naked.
你没穿衣服。

998
00:39:32.720 --> 00:39:33.220
You're naked.
你没穿衣服。

999
00:39:33.380 --> 00:39:35.300
So, don't let it stress you out.
所以，别为此感到压力。

1000
00:39:35.480 --> 00:39:36.400
There's no tipping allowed.
这里不允许给小费。

1001
00:39:36.620 --> 00:39:36.760
Yeah.
是啊。

1002
00:39:37.040 --> 00:39:39.100
Don't worry about where you're carrying the extra cash.
别担心你把多余的现金带在身上。

1003
00:39:39.240 --> 00:39:39.400
Yeah.
是啊。

1004
00:39:39.640 --> 00:39:40.220
Not a problem.
没问题。

1005
00:39:40.660 --> 00:39:45.940
One of the frequently asked questions is, are there irons and ironing boards?
常见问题之一是，那里有熨斗和熨衣板吗？

1006
00:39:47.600 --> 00:39:48.420
For what?
干什么用的？

1007
00:39:49.420 --> 00:39:51.320
I don't know, but the answer is yes.
我不知道，但答案是有的。

1008
00:39:52.600 --> 00:39:55.240
So, yes, they do have irons and ironing boards.
所以，没错，他们确实有熨斗和熨衣板。

1009
00:39:55.700 --> 00:39:56.140
So...
那么……

1010
00:39:56.140 --> 00:39:58.040
Also, you can renew your vows there.
另外，你还可以在那里重温结婚誓词。

1011
00:39:59.060 --> 00:39:59.500
Okay.
好的。

1012
00:39:59.940 --> 00:40:00.540
All right.
行吧。

1013
00:40:00.860 --> 00:40:02.980
Toby suggests that Jim go to Amsterdam.
托比建议吉姆去阿姆斯特丹。

1014
00:40:03.280 --> 00:40:07.560
He says he went there after his divorce for a week or maybe a month.
他说他离婚后去过那里，待了一周或者一个月。

1015
00:40:07.660 --> 00:40:08.480
He can't remember.
他记不清了。

1016
00:40:09.060 --> 00:40:11.380
Creed says he should go to Hong Kong.
克里德说他应该去香港。

1017
00:40:11.580 --> 00:40:15.840
Creed also calls John Jimmy, and I feel like you can see John about to break.
克里德还管约翰叫吉米，我觉得你能看出约翰快要憋不住笑了。

1018
00:40:16.040 --> 00:40:16.720
He's like, Jimmy!
他当时就像是，吉米！

1019
00:40:17.660 --> 00:40:21.140
And I swear, John has this, like, he's kind of got this side smile.
我发誓，约翰当时那种表情，他有点那种侧着嘴笑的样子。

1020
00:40:21.760 --> 00:40:25.540
Well, at 9 minutes, 29 seconds, Creed has a talking head.
嗯，在9分29秒的时候，克里德有一个单人访谈镜头。

1021
00:40:25.740 --> 00:40:29.740
For anyone wondering, Creed is speaking Mandarin.
如果有谁好奇的话，克里德说的是普通话。

1022
00:40:30.140 --> 00:40:30.420
Yeah.
是啊。

1023
00:40:30.680 --> 00:40:33.020
And he says, hello, my Chinese friends.
他说的是，你好，我的中国朋友们。

1024
00:40:33.440 --> 00:40:35.120
That's what he's saying in Mandarin.
这就是他用普通话说的内容。

1025
00:40:35.400 --> 00:40:36.620
I reached out to Creed.
我联系了克里德。

1026
00:40:36.780 --> 00:40:36.980
Yeah?
是吗？

1027
00:40:36.980 --> 00:40:40.060
Because we had a fan question from KKPL Watson.
因为我们收到了粉丝KKPL Watson的一个提问。

1028
00:40:40.680 --> 00:40:45.120
He said, at various times, Creed has spoken Japanese and Chinese on the show.
他说，克里德在剧中多次说过日语和中文。

1029
00:40:45.240 --> 00:40:46.540
Does he really speak either?
他真的会说这两种语言吗？

1030
00:40:47.640 --> 00:40:49.260
So, I texted Creed.
所以我给克里德发了短信。

1031
00:40:49.540 --> 00:40:50.540
Oh, I can't wait.
哦，我等不及了。

1032
00:40:50.620 --> 00:40:51.400
What was his response?
他怎么回的？

1033
00:40:51.660 --> 00:40:52.560
Here's what he said.
他是这么说的。

1034
00:40:52.740 --> 00:40:53.660
Did he say, who are you?
他是不是说，你是谁？

1035
00:40:53.780 --> 00:40:54.080
No.
没有。

1036
00:40:54.080 --> 00:40:55.980
But, again, I wasn't sure.
不过，我还是不太确定。

1037
00:40:56.460 --> 00:41:05.540
He said, when I was in Germany in 1964, I conversed in a rudimentary fashion because I'd studied a year in college.
他说，1964年我在德国的时候，我能进行简单的交流，因为我在大学里学过一年。

1038
00:41:06.060 --> 00:41:08.060
But he said he hasn't used it since.
但他表示从那以后就没再用过了。

1039
00:41:08.580 --> 00:41:18.920
He says he does not speak Japanese or Mandarin or Cantonese, which is actually the language they speak in Hong Kong, mostly, not Mandarin.
他说他不会说日语、普通话或粤语，而粤语其实才是香港人主要说的语言，不是普通话。

1040
00:41:18.920 --> 00:41:24.960
But he said, I do have a made-up language that I've been trying to get accepted.
但他又说，我确实有一种自创的语言，我一直试图让大家接受它。

1041
00:41:25.220 --> 00:41:25.960
That I believe.
这点我信。

1042
00:41:26.140 --> 00:41:31.360
But he's been meeting resistance, and he used it during his stint as manager for that week at Dunder Mifflin.
但他一直遭到抵制，他在邓德·米夫林当经理的那一周里就用过这种语言。

1043
00:41:31.760 --> 00:41:32.720
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1044
00:41:32.920 --> 00:41:33.960
This is Creed, guys.
这就是克里德，伙计们。

1045
00:41:33.980 --> 00:41:34.420
That's Creed.
那就是克里德。

1046
00:41:34.420 --> 00:41:35.040
This is Creed.
这就是克里德。

1047
00:41:40.480 --> 00:41:40.980
All right.
好吧。

1048
00:41:41.060 --> 00:41:44.880
At 9 minutes 57 seconds, my character smiles.
在9分57秒的时候，我的角色笑了。

1049
00:41:45.580 --> 00:41:47.600
This doesn't happen very often.
这种情况并不常发生。

1050
00:41:47.860 --> 00:41:52.400
And, Jenna, I did one of our little dorky actor-y things where I gave myself a backstory.
而且，珍娜，我做了我们演员那种傻乎乎的小动作，我给自己编了个背景故事。

1051
00:41:53.080 --> 00:41:54.280
For this little smile?
就为了这一个小小的微笑？

1052
00:41:54.320 --> 00:41:55.240
For this little moment.
就为了这一个小小的瞬间。

1053
00:41:55.500 --> 00:42:01.420
So it wasn't scripted, but in the conference room, Dwight is going to now do his speech for us.
所以这并不是剧本安排的，但在会议室里，德怀特现在要为我们发表他的演讲了。

1054
00:42:01.620 --> 00:42:02.980
He has his note cards, right?
他拿着他的笔记卡，对吧？

1055
00:42:04.180 --> 00:42:10.320
And I just sort of gave myself this backstory that he had probably practiced this in front of me, that we had worked on it together.
我给自己设定了一个背景故事，那就是他可能在我面前练习过，我们一起排练过。

1056
00:42:10.880 --> 00:42:16.740
And so I just really beam as he gets up there, and I look around to make sure, is everyone watching?
所以当他站起来时，我真的满脸笑意，我环顾四周确认大家都在看吗？

1057
00:42:17.080 --> 00:42:18.440
Because I'm really proud of him.
因为我真的为他感到骄傲。

1058
00:42:18.520 --> 00:42:18.760
Yeah.
是啊。

1059
00:42:18.960 --> 00:42:20.340
So I just had this little thing.
所以我只是做了那个小动作。

1060
00:42:20.340 --> 00:42:28.900
I gave myself, I didn't tell anyone, but Randall and Matt, our camera operators, they caught it, and it made it in.
我给自己加的戏，我没告诉任何人，但我们的摄影师兰德尔和马特捕捉到了，而且被剪进去了。

1061
00:42:29.100 --> 00:42:29.340
Oh.
噢。

1062
00:42:29.400 --> 00:42:30.720
And they would often do that.
他们经常那样做。

1063
00:42:30.860 --> 00:42:36.300
Randall and Matt would sort of catch these little moments that we did in the background that weren't part of the script.
兰德尔和马特会捕捉到我们在背景里做的那些不在剧本里的小动作。

1064
00:42:36.300 --> 00:42:42.820
And they were so great about sort of finding those moments and making sure that everyone saw them.
他们非常擅长发现那些瞬间，并确保每个人都能看到。

1065
00:42:43.040 --> 00:42:45.480
I just like that all of us all the time,
我就是喜欢我们所有人一直以来，

1066
00:42:45.480 --> 00:42:57.080
we were so invested in our characters and how our character would react to a moment or to a story that even if we hadn't been directed or didn't think the camera was on us,
我们都全身心地投入到角色中，思考角色会对某个瞬间或故事做出什么反应，即使导演没有要求，或者我们以为摄像机没对着我们，

1067
00:42:57.200 --> 00:43:00.720
we would stay in our characters and react in the moment.
我们也会保持角色状态，做出当下的反应。

1068
00:43:00.720 --> 00:43:01.140
Yeah.
是啊。

1069
00:43:01.380 --> 00:43:03.840
And that's an example of one of those that made it in.
这就是其中一个被剪进去的例子。

1070
00:43:03.960 --> 00:43:04.160
Yeah.
是啊。

1071
00:43:04.320 --> 00:43:06.960
And I remember Matt saying, Ange, I see what you're doing.
我记得马特说，安吉，我看到你在做什么了。

1072
00:43:07.140 --> 00:43:07.340
Oh.
噢。

1073
00:43:07.340 --> 00:43:08.240
I'm going to clock it.
我会把它记录下来的。

1074
00:43:08.340 --> 00:43:08.900
I caught it.
我捕捉到了。

1075
00:43:09.100 --> 00:43:11.640
That was always so fun when they would notice our little choices.
当他们注意到我们的小设计时，总是特别有趣。

1076
00:43:11.920 --> 00:43:12.160
Yeah.
是啊。

1077
00:43:12.640 --> 00:43:12.920
Aw.
啊。

1078
00:43:13.160 --> 00:43:14.000
I love that.
我喜欢这个。

1079
00:43:14.180 --> 00:43:14.440
Yeah.
是啊。

1080
00:43:15.180 --> 00:43:22.960
Well, then we go to Jim and Dwight's desks, Angela, and Dwight is talking all about the, he's going to go to New Zealand.
好吧，然后我们来到吉姆和德怀特的办公桌前，安吉拉，德怀特正在大谈特谈，他要去新西兰。

1081
00:43:23.860 --> 00:43:24.400
I don't know.
我不知道。

1082
00:43:24.520 --> 00:43:28.140
He tells Jim he should go to New Zealand and walk the Lord of the Rings trail.
他告诉吉姆他应该去新西兰，走一走《指环王》的路线。

1083
00:43:28.360 --> 00:43:28.500
Okay.
好吧。

1084
00:43:28.560 --> 00:43:30.040
I did not understand any of that.
我一点都没听懂。

1085
00:43:30.140 --> 00:43:30.900
Did you understand that?
你听懂了吗？

1086
00:43:30.980 --> 00:43:31.420
Of course I did.
我当然听懂了。

1087
00:43:31.580 --> 00:43:31.800
So Jim.
所以吉姆。

1088
00:43:31.800 --> 00:43:33.160
You knew what all that stuff meant?
你知道那些东西是什么意思？

1089
00:43:33.160 --> 00:43:34.100
I knew what all of it meant, Jenna.
我全都知道是什么意思，珍娜。

1090
00:43:34.300 --> 00:43:37.760
But Jim is like, Dwight, where would you, if you could go anywhere?
但吉姆问，德怀特，如果你能去任何地方，你会去哪？

1091
00:43:38.020 --> 00:43:40.300
And Dwight was like, I can go anywhere and I will.
德怀特说，我可以去任何地方，我也确实会去。

1092
00:43:40.980 --> 00:43:41.140
Yeah.
是啊。

1093
00:43:41.140 --> 00:43:46.980
But one of the places he would like to go is New Zealand because he wants to walk the Lord of the Rings trail to Modor.
但他想去的地方之一是新西兰，因为他想去走《指环王》里去往魔多的路。

1094
00:43:47.340 --> 00:43:47.740
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

1095
00:43:47.940 --> 00:43:48.780
I don't know what that is.
我不知道那是什么。

1096
00:43:48.940 --> 00:43:49.720
Is that a place?
那是个地方吗？

1097
00:43:50.160 --> 00:43:50.600
Modor.
魔多。

1098
00:43:50.820 --> 00:43:52.000
Modor is a castle?
魔多是个城堡吗？

1099
00:43:52.400 --> 00:43:53.320
It's a place.
那是个地方。

1100
00:43:53.580 --> 00:43:56.660
Is it a castle or is it like something hidden under a rock in the ground?
它是城堡，还是像藏在地下岩石里的什么东西？

1101
00:43:57.120 --> 00:43:57.860
It's a place.
那是个地方。

1102
00:43:57.920 --> 00:43:59.100
Is it a village?
是个村庄吗？

1103
00:43:59.320 --> 00:44:00.680
Modor is where Sauron is.
魔多是索伦所在的地方。

1104
00:44:00.800 --> 00:44:01.040
Yeah.
对。

1105
00:44:01.520 --> 00:44:03.040
Sorry, what is Sauron?
抱歉，索伦是什么？

1106
00:44:03.280 --> 00:44:03.720
Sauron.
索伦。

1107
00:44:03.880 --> 00:44:05.160
The Eye of Sauron.
索伦之眼。

1108
00:44:05.300 --> 00:44:06.640
Is that a thing or a person?
那是个东西还是个人？

1109
00:44:06.860 --> 00:44:08.540
I don't know how to describe it.
我不知道该怎么形容它。

1110
00:44:08.600 --> 00:44:09.140
It's pure evil.
它是纯粹的邪恶。

1111
00:44:09.140 --> 00:44:10.920
How can you not describe it?
你怎么会形容不出来呢？

1112
00:44:10.920 --> 00:44:12.460
How do you describe the Eye of Sauron?
你该怎么形容索伦之眼？

1113
00:44:12.620 --> 00:44:16.560
It's like, it's like a, it's like a, like an evil spirit.
它就像，就像个，就像个，就像个邪灵。

1114
00:44:16.920 --> 00:44:17.800
But it's not a person.
但它不是人。

1115
00:44:19.440 --> 00:44:21.360
Sam, how do I explain Eye of Sauron?
山姆，我该怎么解释索伦之眼？

1116
00:44:21.400 --> 00:44:23.180
I think it was, it was a person.
我觉得它曾经，曾经是个人。

1117
00:44:23.180 --> 00:44:26.040
It was a person and he's gaining his power back.
他曾经是个人，而且他正在恢复力量。

1118
00:44:26.160 --> 00:44:26.700
And then he'll be.
然后他就会。

1119
00:44:26.700 --> 00:44:28.340
If he gets to the ring, then he can be a person again.
如果他拿到了戒指，他就能变回人。

1120
00:44:28.360 --> 00:44:32.720
Then he can be fully complete and he will reign pure hell all over the land.
那样他就能完全复活，并在整片土地上散布纯粹的恐怖。

1121
00:44:33.580 --> 00:44:39.640
So your difficulty in explaining it to me is why I don't like to watch it.
所以你很难向我解释清楚，这就是我不想看的原因。

1122
00:44:39.780 --> 00:44:40.420
Well, I'm not.
好吧，我不是。

1123
00:44:40.420 --> 00:44:42.680
Because it's like, I don't, I'm not.
因为这就像，我不知道，我不是。

1124
00:44:42.740 --> 00:44:43.780
So convoluted.
太复杂了。

1125
00:44:44.040 --> 00:44:45.600
I'm not as versed in Lord of the Rings.
我对《指环王》没那么了解。

1126
00:44:45.900 --> 00:44:46.260
Okay.
好吧。

1127
00:44:46.440 --> 00:44:46.880
All right.
行吧。

1128
00:44:47.060 --> 00:44:50.640
But I do know that the trail to Modor and.
但我确实知道去魔多的路，还有。

1129
00:44:50.800 --> 00:44:51.940
Why would you want to go there?
你为什么想去那儿？

1130
00:44:52.120 --> 00:44:55.360
Why are people trying to go to Modor or not trying to go to Modor?
为什么人们想去魔多，或者不想去魔多？

1131
00:44:55.380 --> 00:44:56.120
You don't want to go there.
你根本不想去那儿。

1132
00:44:56.120 --> 00:44:57.520
Why, so why does Dwight want to go there?
那为什么，为什么德怀特想去那儿？

1133
00:44:57.520 --> 00:45:00.180
I mean, there's like lava fields and all this kind of craziness.
我是说，那儿有熔岩地带之类的疯狂景象。

1134
00:45:00.540 --> 00:45:01.800
And then hike Mount Doom.
还要徒步攀登末日火山。

1135
00:45:01.940 --> 00:45:04.280
I think Dwight is like a huge Lord of the Rings fan.
我觉得德怀特是个超级《指环王》迷。

1136
00:45:04.460 --> 00:45:07.020
He basically wants to be one of the Lord of the Rings.
他基本上是想成为指环王里的一员。

