他受不了德怀特表现得那么好。

1468
00:57:46.450 --> 00:57:50.250
I bet probably people never reacted like that to Michael's speech.
我敢说，大家以前肯定没对迈克尔的演讲有过这种反应。

1469
00:57:50.250 --> 00:57:52.850
Which, like, people were not, like, hooting and hollering.
也就是说，大家当时并没有欢呼雀跃。

1470
00:57:53.130 --> 00:57:53.330
No.
没有。

1471
00:57:53.670 --> 00:57:53.910
Yeah.
是啊。

1472
00:57:54.410 --> 00:57:56.990
So Michael, he's sitting at the bar.
所以迈克尔坐在酒吧里。

1473
00:57:57.090 --> 00:58:05.970
Eventually Dwight comes out, and he finds him, and he starts telling him a story about some woman who sat there who didn't have her ID.
后来德怀特出来了，找到了他，开始跟他讲一个女人坐在那儿没带身份证的故事。

1474
00:58:06.330 --> 00:58:08.010
But Dwight's so into it.
但德怀特讲得太投入了。

1475
00:58:08.030 --> 00:58:11.110
Dwight immediately clicks into Michael's story.
德怀特立刻就进入了迈克尔的故事节奏。

1476
00:58:11.250 --> 00:58:11.430
Yeah.
没错。

1477
00:58:11.590 --> 00:58:16.990
And Michael has this quote where he says, listen, I captivated the guy who captivated a thousand guys.
迈克尔当时说了句名言，他说，听着，我征服了那个征服了千人的男人。

1478
00:58:17.590 --> 00:58:19.850
So, like, who's the winner today?
那么，谁才是今天的赢家呢？

1479
00:58:19.850 --> 00:58:20.490
Who's the winner?
谁是赢家？

1480
00:58:20.810 --> 00:58:25.050
Okay, so, Ange, I had a fan question from Madeline Ethington.
好了，安吉，我收到一个来自玛德琳·埃辛顿的粉丝提问。

1481
00:58:25.610 --> 00:58:26.170
Okay.
好的。

1482
00:58:26.710 --> 00:58:29.910
This, I've never loved male more than this male.
这个，我从来没像现在这样喜欢过男性。

1483
00:58:30.090 --> 00:58:31.610
Okay, Madeline, wow.
好吧，玛德琳，哇。

1484
00:58:31.850 --> 00:58:38.130
Madeline wrote and said, I have been waiting for this episode to ask this question.
玛德琳写信说，我一直等着这一集来问这个问题。

1485
00:58:38.130 --> 00:58:39.350
What is it, Madeline?
是什么问题，玛德琳？

1486
00:58:39.350 --> 00:58:48.330
At 20 minutes and 25 seconds, when Michael and Dwight are sitting at the bar, you can see a man in the background dressed like a wizard.
在20分25秒的时候，当迈克尔和德怀特坐在酒吧里时，你可以看到背景里有个男人打扮成巫师的样子。

1487
00:58:49.630 --> 00:58:51.390
Why is he there?
他为什么在那儿？

1488
00:58:51.750 --> 00:58:52.350
Why?
为什么？

1489
00:58:52.770 --> 00:58:53.910
Was it planned?
是计划好的吗？

1490
00:58:54.090 --> 00:58:55.170
Was it an accident?
还是个意外？

1491
00:58:55.530 --> 00:58:58.930
And then she just wrote again, who is that wizard?
然后她又写道，那个巫师到底是谁？

1492
00:58:59.170 --> 00:59:00.690
I know the answer to this.
我知道答案。

1493
00:59:00.770 --> 00:59:01.310
I do too.
我也知道。

1494
00:59:01.810 --> 00:59:03.910
But I didn't know.
但我之前不知道。

1495
00:59:04.730 --> 00:59:08.510
I went, I was like, this is the strangest question.
我当时想，这问题也太奇怪了。

1496
00:59:08.730 --> 00:59:12.570
I went to 20 minutes, 25 seconds, and I laughed out loud.
我看了20分25秒的那段，直接笑出声来。

1497
00:59:12.730 --> 00:59:13.630
Can we see it?
我们能看看吗？

1498
00:59:13.750 --> 00:59:15.150
Full head-to-toe wizard.
从头到脚全套巫师装扮。

1499
00:59:15.390 --> 00:59:15.790
Well.
好吧。

1500
00:59:15.790 --> 00:59:16.750
I took a picture.
我拍了张照片。

1501
00:59:16.970 --> 00:59:17.950
You have to show me.
你得给我展示一下。

1502
00:59:18.090 --> 00:59:21.250
I know why, but I know why because I watched the deleted scenes.
我知道原因，但我知道是因为我看了删减片段。

1503
00:59:22.030 --> 00:59:29.930
Oh, I know why because I asked Kent Sabornak and Paul Lieberstein, why is there a man dressed as a wizard in the background?
噢，我知道原因，因为我问过肯特·萨博纳克和保罗·李伯斯坦，为什么背景里有个穿成巫师的人？

1504
00:59:30.130 --> 00:59:30.450
Okay.
好吧。

1505
00:59:30.770 --> 00:59:34.190
So you tell me what you found out, and I'll tell you what I found out.
所以你告诉我你发现了什么，我再告诉你我发现了什么。

1506
00:59:34.370 --> 00:59:35.630
Here he is, Angela.
他在这儿呢，安吉拉。

1507
00:59:35.970 --> 00:59:36.230
Yeah.
是啊。

1508
00:59:36.410 --> 00:59:37.830
He's got a name tag on.
他戴着名牌呢。

1509
00:59:38.070 --> 00:59:38.550
Okay.
好吧。

1510
00:59:38.950 --> 00:59:43.790
Well, obviously, I don't know Kent and Paul's answer, but I watched the deleted scenes,
嗯，显然我不知道肯特和保罗的回答，但我看了删减片段，

1511
00:59:43.790 --> 00:59:51.090
and there is an extended scene of them walking through the hotel where the convention centers are.
里面有一段他们穿过会议中心所在酒店的加长片段。

1512
00:59:51.250 --> 00:59:51.490
Okay.
好吧。

1513
00:59:51.590 --> 00:59:56.310
And they go up to the very first one they see, and they walk in, and it's the wrong one.
他们走到看到的第一个房间，走进去，结果走错了。

1514
00:59:56.530 --> 00:59:56.870
Oh.
噢。

1515
00:59:56.950 --> 01:00:00.070
And it's like just some random convention.
那只是个随便什么会议。

1516
01:00:00.510 --> 01:00:09.710
And then they go into a second room, and it's like all of these cosplay people who are dressed like characters from things.
然后他们进了第二个房间，里面全是那些打扮成各种角色的人。

1517
01:00:09.870 --> 01:00:10.190
Oh.
噢。

1518
01:00:10.390 --> 01:00:13.730
And Dwight's like, oh, I wish I, oh, I wanted to go to this.
德怀特说，噢，我真希望，噢，我本来想去这个的。

1519
01:00:13.850 --> 01:00:14.870
It has like a whole name.
它好像有个完整的名字。

1520
01:00:14.970 --> 01:00:15.270
Damn it.
该死。

1521
01:00:15.370 --> 01:00:16.130
I'm forgetting the name.
我忘了名字了。

1522
01:00:16.270 --> 01:00:18.250
But Dwight was like, I would have gone.
但德怀特说，我本来会去的。

1523
01:00:18.250 --> 01:00:22.990
And then he's like, I really hope I see the gal from Battlestar Galactica.
然后他说，我真希望我能见到《太空堡垒卡拉狄加》里的那个姑娘。

1524
01:00:23.110 --> 01:00:23.730
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1525
01:00:23.730 --> 01:00:24.770
She's so hot.
她太辣了。

1526
01:00:25.070 --> 01:00:25.290
Okay.
好吧。

1527
01:00:25.410 --> 01:00:35.290
This must have been improvised because Kent told me that their location agreement with the Sheridan allowed them to shoot basically anywhere on the property.
这肯定是即兴发挥的，因为肯特告诉我，他们与喜来登酒店的场地协议允许他们在酒店内几乎任何地方拍摄。

1528
01:00:35.290 --> 01:00:39.870
But the only room they were allowed to shut down and control was that ballroom.
但他们唯一被允许封闭和控制的房间就是那个宴会厅。

1529
01:00:40.150 --> 01:00:40.290
Yeah.
是啊。

1530
01:00:41.210 --> 01:00:49.650
And otherwise, they just had those signs up that said, if you walk in this area, you might be filmed for a TV show.
除此之外，他们只是立了些牌子，上面写着，如果你走进这个区域，你可能会被拍进电视节目里。

1531
01:00:49.850 --> 01:00:54.150
And by walking in this area, you give permission to be on the TV show.
并且走进这个区域，即视为你同意出现在电视节目中。

1532
01:00:54.390 --> 01:00:58.430
I don't know if you guys outside of L.A., you see these signs a lot around town.
我不知道你们洛杉矶以外的人，你们在城里经常看到这种牌子吗？

1533
01:00:58.510 --> 01:00:59.650
Because you're just living your life.
因为你只是在过自己的生活。

1534
01:00:59.650 --> 01:01:05.670
And there's like a sign, and you're like, oh, they're filming on the street, and I'm going to be in the background getting my coffee, I guess.
然后有个牌子，你会想，噢，他们在街上拍戏，我想我会被拍进背景里去买咖啡吧。

1535
01:01:06.570 --> 01:01:16.130
So, they had these signs up, and he said that they just had to allow public access while they were rolling, and there was an anime expo in one of the other ballrooMs.
所以，他们立了这些牌子，他说他们拍摄时必须允许公众进入，而另一个宴会厅里正好有个动漫展。

1536
01:01:16.390 --> 01:01:16.790
Yes.
没错。

1537
01:01:16.930 --> 01:01:18.110
With people dressed up.
还有人打扮成那样。

1538
01:01:18.110 --> 01:01:24.310
So, I guess then Rain and Steve improvised this whole thing that it was like a cosplay convention.
所以，我想雷恩和史蒂夫当时即兴发挥，把这编成了个角色扮演大会。

1539
01:01:24.450 --> 01:01:25.110
They must have.
他们一定是即兴的。

1540
01:01:25.190 --> 01:01:30.270
And Rain was really, really bummed because, well, Dwight was really bummed because he had wanted to go to it.
雷恩当时真的很沮丧，因为，嗯，德怀特真的很沮丧，因为他本来想去参加那个展的。

1541
01:01:31.510 --> 01:01:37.030
And supposedly, there was a Battlestar Galactica cast member that was going to be there, and he was like really excited.
而且据说《太空堡垒卡拉狄加》的一位演员会去那里，他当时真的很兴奋。

1542
01:01:37.290 --> 01:01:38.450
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1543
01:01:38.870 --> 01:01:46.570
Well, both Kent and Paul said a version of the same thing, which was they really tried to avoid getting the dressed up people in the shots.
嗯，肯特和保罗说的版本差不多，他们确实尽量避免把那些打扮的人拍进镜头里。

1544
01:01:46.570 --> 01:01:49.330
But this one wizard managed to get on camera.
但这个巫师还是设法闯进了镜头。

1545
01:01:49.510 --> 01:01:55.250
And maybe they had to film that little improv to justify it if they, like too many of them showed up at one time.
也许他们不得不拍那段即兴表演来圆场，以防太多人同时出现。

1546
01:01:55.330 --> 01:01:56.550
Yeah, that's amazing.
是啊，太神奇了。

1547
01:01:56.970 --> 01:02:01.270
The hotel in the show is supposedly the Radisson Lackawanna Station Hotel.
剧中的酒店据说是拉迪森拉卡瓦纳车站酒店。

1548
01:02:01.530 --> 01:02:01.770
Okay.
好吧。

1549
01:02:01.990 --> 01:02:02.910
I have stayed there.
我住过那里。

1550
01:02:03.150 --> 01:02:03.650
Oh!
噢！

1551
01:02:04.130 --> 01:02:06.010
We stayed there for the convention.
我们当时是为了参加大会住在那儿的。

1552
01:02:06.350 --> 01:02:10.710
There was an office convention in 2007, and that's where the whole cast stayed.
2007年有个办公室大会，整个剧组都住在那儿。

1553
01:02:10.770 --> 01:02:11.770
And it's a lovely hotel.
那是一家很棒的酒店。

1554
01:02:16.570 --> 01:02:20.470
And they have, you know, fixed it up and made it into this hotel, and it's really nice.
他们翻新了那里，把它改造成了现在的酒店，真的很好。

1555
01:02:20.470 --> 01:02:24.970
So if you're in Scranton, I recommend the Radisson Lackawanna Station Hotel.
所以如果你去斯克兰顿，我推荐雷迪森拉卡瓦纳车站酒店。

1556
01:02:25.590 --> 01:02:32.210
Well, when the finale happened, a bunch of us went to Scranton for a big parade, and we stayed there as well.
在大结局的时候，我们一群人去斯克兰顿参加大游行，我们也住在那儿。

1557
01:02:32.330 --> 01:02:34.870
So I've also stayed there, and I concur.
所以我也住过那儿，我表示赞同。

1558
01:02:35.170 --> 01:02:36.130
It's a great hotel.
那是一家很棒的酒店。

1559
01:02:36.310 --> 01:02:36.850
Great hotel.
很棒的酒店。

1560
01:02:37.010 --> 01:02:37.590
Super charming.
超级迷人。

1561
01:02:37.730 --> 01:02:38.410
Super charming.
超级迷人。

1562
01:02:38.410 --> 01:02:41.810
So now Dwight and Michael are sort of having this great moment at the bar.
现在德怀特和迈克尔在酒吧里度过了一段很棒的时光。

1563
01:02:41.990 --> 01:02:44.870
They're laughing, and it's all wrapping up.
他们在大笑，一切都要结束了。

1564
01:02:44.970 --> 01:02:49.250
But guess who's the last person to touch the thermostat back in the office?
但你猜办公室里最后一个碰恒温器的人是谁？

1565
01:02:50.150 --> 01:02:50.830
Who?
谁？

1566
01:02:51.350 --> 01:02:51.790
Creed.
克里德。

1567
01:02:52.510 --> 01:02:53.990
Why did I miss that?
我怎么没注意到？

1568
01:02:54.190 --> 01:02:57.830
Creed goes over there and adjusts the thermostat.
克里德走过去调了恒温器。

1569
01:02:58.030 --> 01:02:59.730
He's the last one.
他是最后一个。

1570
01:02:59.750 --> 01:03:01.310
I missed that.
我没注意到。

1571
01:03:02.230 --> 01:03:12.470
Well, at the very end of this episode, Jim is passing by Pam's desk, and Pam says, oh, I've always wanted to go to Australia.
在这一集的最后，吉姆经过帕姆的办公桌，帕姆说，哦，我一直想去澳大利亚。

1572
01:03:13.010 --> 01:03:14.450
And he says, well, I'm going.
他说，好吧，我要去了。

1573
01:03:14.450 --> 01:03:16.230
I bought a non-refundable ticket.
我买了张不可退款的票。

1574
01:03:16.590 --> 01:03:21.810
And this is when he tells us he bought his ticket for June 8th.
就在这时他告诉我们他买了6月8号的票。

1575
01:03:22.010 --> 01:03:23.990
Oh, the look on Pam's face.
哦，帕姆脸上的表情。

1576
01:03:23.990 --> 01:03:25.670
Her wedding is June 10th.
她的婚礼是6月10号。

1577
01:03:25.670 --> 01:03:27.690
I mean, this is so telling.
我是说，这太能说明问题了。

1578
01:03:27.910 --> 01:03:35.930
I mean, Pam, if Pam had any doubts at all that this was hard on him, she can't deny it anymore.
我是说，帕姆，如果帕姆之前对这件事让他感到痛苦还有任何怀疑的话，现在她无法再否认了。

1579
01:03:36.070 --> 01:03:37.030
Yeah, he's leaving.
是啊，他要走了。

1580
01:03:37.270 --> 01:03:43.270
He has basically said to her, I'm sorry, but I cannot be there when you marry someone else.
他基本上是在告诉她，对不起，当你嫁给别人的时候，我无法在场。

1581
01:03:43.390 --> 01:03:44.270
I can't be there.
我无法在场。

1582
01:03:44.470 --> 01:03:51.610
In fact, I have to be on basically the farthest spot on the earth from your wedding.
事实上，我必须去地球上离你婚礼最远的地方。

1583
01:03:51.730 --> 01:03:51.890
Yeah.
是啊。

1584
01:03:51.890 --> 01:03:56.670
I'm going to go halfway around the world to get away from your wedding.
我要去地球的另一端，远离你的婚礼。

1585
01:03:56.890 --> 01:03:59.670
I mean, it just gutted me.
我是说，这真的让我心碎。

1586
01:03:59.810 --> 01:04:04.750
And I just wanted to shake Pam and be like, if you don't know now, then you'll never know.
我真想摇醒帕姆，告诉她，如果你现在还不明白，那你永远都不会明白了。

1587
01:04:04.770 --> 01:04:05.790
He loves you.
他爱你。

1588
01:04:06.070 --> 01:04:07.690
But I think it's more than that.
但我认为不仅仅是这样。

1589
01:04:07.830 --> 01:04:16.250
I think what's happening is Jim is saying, I'm not sure how to even be your friend now that you're getting married.
我觉得吉姆是在说，既然你要结婚了，我甚至不知道该怎么做你的朋友了。

1590
01:04:16.250 --> 01:04:22.710
Like, I know we're best friends at the office, but I'm not going to come to your wedding.
我知道我们在办公室是最好的朋友，但我不会去参加你的婚礼。

1591
01:04:22.710 --> 01:04:26.810
And when you're married, I'm not going to hang with you.
等你结婚后，我也不会再和你混在一起了。

1592
01:04:27.310 --> 01:04:28.550
He's, you know.
他，你知道的。

1593
01:04:28.750 --> 01:04:32.390
I think what he's finally admitting is they're not best friends.
我想他最终承认的是，他们并不是最好的朋友。

1594
01:04:32.610 --> 01:04:33.430
Yeah, they can't.
是啊，他们做不到。

1595
01:04:33.430 --> 01:04:34.630
How can they be?
他们怎么可能做到呢？

1596
01:04:34.870 --> 01:04:36.470
They've crossed this line.
他们已经越界了。

1597
01:04:36.730 --> 01:04:38.430
They've had that moment on Booze Cruise.
他们在“酒水游轮”上经历过那一刻。

1598
01:04:38.870 --> 01:04:42.530
They've had these moments now, and the line has been crossed.
他们现在有了这些时刻，界限已经被打破了。

1599
01:04:42.710 --> 01:04:42.830
Yeah.
是啊。

1600
01:04:44.030 --> 01:04:47.650
And now they're in this uncharted territory of, like, what do we do now?
现在他们进入了一个未知的领域，就像，我们现在该怎么办？

1601
01:04:48.430 --> 01:04:49.870
What's next week's episode?
下周的剧集是什么？

1602
01:04:50.070 --> 01:04:51.830
Take Your Daughter to Work Day, I think.
我想是“带女儿上班日”。

1603
01:04:52.030 --> 01:04:52.210
Yeah.
没错。

1604
01:04:52.690 --> 01:04:53.250
Oh, boy.
天哪。

1605
01:04:53.690 --> 01:04:56.190
This is when, you guys, I was wrong.
伙计们，这次是我错了。

1606
01:04:56.330 --> 01:04:56.770
Okay?
好吗？

1607
01:04:56.770 --> 01:04:57.870
I used the shredder.
我用了碎纸机。

1608
01:04:59.130 --> 01:05:00.670
Oh, okay.
哦，好吧。

1609
01:05:01.070 --> 01:05:01.510
All right.
行吧。

1610
01:05:01.510 --> 01:05:05.250
So I'll get the time code for that so I can really lay into myself.
我会找出那段的时间码，这样我就能好好数落自己一番了。

1611
01:05:05.490 --> 01:05:07.930
Yeah, Take Your Daughter to Work Day is coming up next week.
没错，“带女儿上班日”下周就要播了。

1612
01:05:08.110 --> 01:05:10.250
All right, you guys, that was Dwight's speech.
好了，伙计们，刚才那是德怀特的演讲。

